  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between the Influenza B virus B/Hong Kong/259/2010 hemagglutinin antigen and Alpha-enolase, mediated through the compound Selgantolimod. This connection is supported by three distinct paths, all of which indicate that the virus antigen is targeted by Selgantolimod, which in turn targets Alpha-enolase. The shared involvement of Selgantolimod as a common mediator across different targets highlights a possible mechanism of action where the virus antigen is indirectly linked to Alpha-enolase through the action of this compound. The evidence is consistent and suggests that Selgantolimod may act as a bridge between the virus antigen and Alpha-enolase, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be elucidated. The presence of multiple pathways with similar scores supports the hypothesis that the relationship is robust, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction.",
